{"text": "§lJoulesmith§r
A tech mod in five tiers: Basic, Reinforced, Advanced, Elite and Ultimate.

Every block's tooltip says what it does, and JEI shows every recipe and an info page for each machine."}

{"text": "§lGetting started§r
Mine tin, lead, silver, nickel and uranium. Smelt raw ore for ingots.

Build a Combustion Generator: it burns furnace fuel for power (FE). Join it to machines with Energy Cables."}

{"text": "§lTiers§r
A Basic Circuit opens tier 2 and an Advanced Circuit tier 3 (Circuit Assembler). A Processor opens tier 4 and a Quantum Processor tier 5 (Laser Engraver).

Upgrade Kits raise cables, pipes, batteries, crates, bins, tanks and solar panels a tier where they stand."}

{"text": "§lMachines§r
Each has slide-out tabs: redstone mode, side settings (input, output, both, off) and upgrade slots for Speed, Efficiency, Bonus, Eject and Range cards.

Hover the red bar to see FE/t."}

{"text": "§lThe Wrench§r
Right-click a machine to turn it. Right-click a pipe or cable side to switch it between connected, push, pull and off.

Hold it to see each machine face's side setting in colour."}

{"text": "§lPipes§r
Item Ducts, Fluid Pipes and Energy Cables connect on their own. Set a side to pull to take from an inventory.

Put a Filter Card on a duct side to choose what passes: by item, tag or mod."}

{"text": "§lRubber and plastic§r
Rubber trees grow in forests and jungles. Tap a log with a Tree Tap for latex; smelt it into rubber.

The Fluid Mixer makes plastic from Biofuel and latex, or from oil."}

{"text": "§lFarming§r
Planters, Harvesters and Tree Farms work the area in front of them. Sprinklers speed growth. Hydroponic Beds grow crops indoors.

The Mob Grinder stores XP as Liquid XP for the Auto Enchanter."}

{"text": "§lAutomation§r
Block Placer, Block Breaker, Autocrafter, Mechanical User, Quarry and Mob Fighter.

Sensors give redstone from what they read; a Logic Controller turns readings into signals."}

{"text": "§lPowered gear§r
The Power Drill, Chainsaw, Energy Sword and Exo-Suit run on FE instead of durability.

Charge them on a Charging Pad or by carrying an Energy Cell."}

{"text": "§lModules§r
At the Modification Table, fit modules to a powered item (two; four or six on Elite and Ultimate Exo-Suits): Fortune, Silk Touch, Range, Magnet, Jetpack, Night Vision, Lifesteal and more.

Each module's tooltip says what it fits."}

{"text": "§lFission§r
Build a 3x3x3 shell of Reactor Casing, Glass and Ports with the Fission Reactor in the middle of one face and the very middle empty.

Feed it uranium and water. It never explodes: with no water it shuts down safely."}

{"text": "§lFusion§r
Make deuterium from water and tritium from deuterium and uranium dust in the Fluid Mixer.

The Fusion Core needs 500,000 FE to light, then makes 20,000 FE/t and plasma for the Plasma Refinery."}

{"text": "§lWireless§r
Dye a Wireless Transmitter and Receiver the same colour: the Receiver draws power from Transmitters on its channel within 256 blocks.

The Wireless Terminal opens a storage network from 64 blocks away."}

{"text": "§lStorage network§r
Cable a Network Core (powered), Drive Bays with Item and Fluid Drives, and a Network Terminal together.

Import and Export Buses move things in and out; filters choose what."}

{"text": "§lAuto-crafting§r
Lay out a recipe in a Crafting Terminal and press Encode to record it on a Blank Pattern. Put Patterns in an Auto-Crafting CPU.

Middle-click an item in a terminal to have it crafted."}

{"text": "§lTier 4 and 5 gear§r
Omni-Tool, Railgun and Plasma Cannon. Upgrade Exo-Suit pieces to Elite and Ultimate at a Smithing Table; modules and charge carry over.

The Drone Hub's drones fetch drops and harvest crops."}
